luix.props.markdownDescription:
Per-class prop list. Each entry overrides the built-in defaults for that class — presence of a key is authoritative, so an explicit empty array (`[]`) disables completions for that class. Custom component identifiers (e.g. `MyButton`) can be added here too. Two shapes:

```jsonc
{
  // Array form: just the prop list.
  "TextLabel": ["Text", "TextColor3"],
  "MyButton": ["label", "onClick", "disabled"],
  // Object form: extend a class and add extras.
  "GamepassCard": { "extends": "Frame", "props": ["gamepassId"] }
}
```

Most custom components don't need this — the extension can usually infer props from in-file annotations, typed signatures, or the component's root `createElement` call. Use config when the component lives in a file the extension can't reach or when you want central overrides.

luix.palette.markdownDescription:
Project palette: named colors that appear as completions when you type `Color3.`. Each value should be the full Roblox expression to insert. Example:

```jsonc
{
  "luix.palette": {
    "primary":    "Color3.fromRGB(124, 92, 255)",
    "background": "Color3.fromRGB(21, 21, 26)",
    "surface":    "Color3.fromRGB(28, 30, 38)",
    "text":       "Color3.fromRGB(255, 255, 255)"
  }
}
```

Typing `BackgroundColor3 = Color3.` then `palette.primary` inserts the full `Color3.fromRGB(124, 92, 255)` expression.

luix.robloxGlyphs.custom.markdownDescription:
Your own `:slug:` shortcuts for characters your keyboard can't reach. Keys are slugs typed between colons inside a string, values are the literal text inserted on accept. Slugs that collide with the built-in glyphs (`robux`, `premium`, `verified`, `roblox-plus`) are ignored.

Example:

```jsonc
{
  "luix.robloxGlyphs.custom": {
    "gbp":  "£",
    "euro": "€",
    "yen":  "¥",
    "shrug": "¯\\_(ツ)_/¯"
  }
}
```

Then typing `:gbp:` inside a string and accepting inserts `£`.

luix.spacing.markdownDescription:
Named spacing tokens that surface as completions when you type `UDim.`. Each value should be the full Roblox expression to insert.

```jsonc
{
  "luix.spacing": {
    "xs": "UDim.new(0, 4)",
    "sm": "UDim.new(0, 8)",
    "md": "UDim.new(0, 16)",
    "lg": "UDim.new(0, 24)"
  }
}
```

Mirror of `luix.palette` for `Color3`.

luix.fonts.markdownDescription:
Named font tokens that surface as completions when you type `Font.`. Each value should be the full Roblox expression to insert.

```jsonc
{
  "luix.fonts": {
    "display": "Font.fromName(\"Gotham\", Enum.FontWeight.Bold)",
    "body":    "Font.fromName(\"SourceSansPro\", Enum.FontWeight.Regular)"
  }
}
```

luix.customFonts.markdownDescription:
Custom Roblox font families and their supported weights, surfaced in the same `Font.fromName("…")` and `Enum.FontWeight.` completions as the built-in catalog. Useful when you've uploaded your own font assets and registered them as a family. Keys are the family name string you pass to `Font.fromName`; values are the list of weights the family ships. Invalid weight names (anything not in the `FontWeight` enum) are silently filtered.

```jsonc
{
  "luix.customFonts": {
    "MyBrandSans":  ["Light", "Regular", "Medium", "Bold"],
    "MyBrandSerif": ["Regular", "Bold"]
  }
}
```

Custom entries surface above built-ins in the dropdown and are tagged *Custom font* in the suggest details. If a custom family shares a name with a built-in, the custom weight list wins.
